  "result": "Here's a draft (about 95 words). I haven't added it to `README.md`.\n\n```markdown\n## Carriers\n\nEach shipping carrier has its own module in `shop/carriers/`, one file per\ncarrier (`acme.py`, `borealis.py`, \u2026 `tundra.py`), 20 in all. Every module\ndefines a `BASE_RATE` constant: a flat charge in cents that is added to the\nweight-based charge. The `rate(weight, zone)` method then applies a zone factor.\n\nAll carriers take weight in kilograms except **Maple** (`shop/carriers/maple.py`),\nwhich takes **grams**. It uses `PER_GRAMS` and `MAX_GRAMS` (max 30,000 g)\ninstead of `PER_KG` and `MAX_KG`. Convert the weight before calling it: passing\nkilograms to Maple will give a quote that is far too low.\n```\n\nEvery carrier file defines `BASE_RATE` on line 7, and Maple's docstring and constants confirm it's the only one using grams. I can add the section to `README.md` if you want it there.",
